    "source": "first assistant implementation notes; unverified; immutable Planner takes precedence",
    "text": "Implementation contract (short):\n\n- Requirement indices -> owning files:\n  - All requirements implemented in game/tower_tiles.py (main game loop, state, rendering, input).\n  - game/__init__.py: package initializer (empty).\n\n- State ownership and interfaces:\n  - Game class (game/tower_tiles.py) owns all global state: grid, path, blobs, towers, coins, lives, wave, timers, game_state.\n  - Public methods:\n    - Game.restart() -> None : resets all state to initial values.\n    - Game.send_next_wave() -> None : starts the next wave immediately.\n    - Game.build_tower(col:int, row:int) -> bool : attempts build; returns True if built.\n  - Blob and Tower classes internal; no cross-file calls.\n\n- Coordinate/convention:\n  - Grid uses (col, row) integers with origin (0,0) at top-left of play area (below UI).\n  - Tile size computed from resolution and UI height; world positions are pixel centers.\n  - Distances for tower range measured in tile units (Euclidean).\n\n- Input -> action -> state -> feedback examples:\n  - KEYDOWN K_RIGHT -> selection.col +=1 -> print \"MOVE RIGHT\" -> selection drawn moved.\n  - KEYDOWN K_SPACE -> Game.build_tower if grass and coins>=50 -> coins-=50 -> tower added -> print \"BUILD\" -> tower rendered.\n  - Tower auto-shoot every 1s -> nearest blob within 2 tiles -> blob.hp -=1 -> if hp==0 coins+=20 and blob removed -> visible removal and console \"[EVENT] COINS:<n>\".\n  - Blob reaches path end -> lives -=1 -> blob removed -> when lives==0 -> print \"GAME OVER\" and freeze updates.\n\n- Lifecycle:\n  - init: Game() constructs initial grid, path, sets coins=150, lives=10, wave=1.\n  - play: running updates blobs and towers if game_state == 'playing'.\n  - terminal: 'won' or 'lost' freeze updates; accept R to restart and ESCAPE to quit.\n  - restart: Game.restart() reconstructs all objects and timers, sets game_state 'playing'.\n\nNow I'll write the promised files.",
    "truncated": false
  },
